# Line endings, decided here rather than by whoever cloned the repository.
#
# Git for Windows installs with `core.autocrlf=true` by default, which rewrites
# every text file to CRLF on checkout. For most of this repository that is
# harmless. For four kinds of file it is not, and the failures do not name their
# cause:
#
#   docker/entrypoint.sh    a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for the
#                           interpreter "/bin/sh\r", and the container exits
#                           with "no such file or directory" naming a path that
#                           obviously exists.
#   Dockerfile, *.mjs bins  a `#!/usr/bin/env node\r` line fails the same way
#                           when the file is executed directly on Linux.
#   *.sql migrations        checksums are computed over file contents; CRLF
#                           makes the same migration a different one.
#   snapshot fixtures       a diff that is entirely invisible.
#
# `create-flowcms` copies the template byte for byte, so whatever a contributor
# has on disk is what every generated project gets. This file ships with the
# template for that reason: an operator who commits their new site and clones it
# on Windows must not get a container that will not start.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything executed by a kernel or an image build. LF is not a preference here.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.cjs           text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.tsx           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
gitignore       text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf

# Binary, and never to be "fixed". Reading a PNG as text to normalise its line
# endings corrupts it in a way no test that does not open the file will catch.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.webp          binary
*.svg           text eol=lf
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.db            binary
*.tgz           binary
*.lockb         binary
